format session-log-v1
stamp 20260814.134526
editor Zed
model Fable 5
voice Kyri
host cloud pier (Eastern / EDT time convention)
title ALES22 — Lotus's cue sheet, the marker track travels as text
prompt Autonomous loop past REMEMBER + the itineraries — take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve the design round, send each finished increment, stop at the custody gates. baton prin recur.
think ALES20 gave named places, ALES21 let them be set in seconds, yet every marker lives only in process memory — close the session and the verse, chorus, edit point are gone. The highest-Lindy next move is PERSISTENCE: a whole markers track rendered as shareable text and parsed back to exactly the same track. The audio world's own word is a cue sheet — a list of named time positions handed from one hand to the next. Lindy-first: persistence outlives every in-session gesture, a keeper's marks are worth keeping; crux-first: it mirrors a proven idiom (HUNK31 render_book/parse_book) and reuses ALES20's one add path, least risk of the road-on's rungs. Wholly local — text in, text out, no seam, no gate.
think The crux and why it is EXACT: parse(render(m)) recovers every position and name byte-for-byte and render(parse(render(m))) is a fixed point. Render walks the strictly-ascending track in order, so the text is canonical (positions ascending, decimal no leading zero) with no per-render drift. Parse hands each line's position and name to markers.add, so the parsed track is sorted, unique, within the master, and within the ceiling by ALES20's own maintained invariant — every bound enforced AT THE TEXT EDGE rather than re-spelled: a corrupt record refuses Duplicate/PastEnd/BadName/MarkersFull by the track's own name before a byte is trusted.
think Reuse over reinvention: markers.add/pos_of/name_of reused whole (markers.rye untouched); the position parsed through tally/parse_int.rye strict decimal (a leading zero refuses, so 007 never masquerades as 7). Added a lotus/parse_int.rye symlink to the canonical tally/parse_int.rye (the same pattern image/ uses). The name is the remainder of the line, so a marker named with a space (the chorus) round-trips whole. New module carries its own two edge errors (Overflow, BadRecord) unioned with markers.MarkerError. No usize, no @memcpy (render via std.fmt.bufPrint), no qualified assert.
think First build GREEN — no witness catch this round. The bounded record size max_sheet_bytes is proven from the header plus max_markers lines each header+widest-u32+name+newline, so render into a well-sized buffer never overruns and a too-small buffer refuses Overflow.
obs GREEN on the first build across six cases: a four-marker track rendered to the exact expected format lotus-cue-sheet-v1 text and parsed back byte-for-byte (positions and names), the render a fixed point; a SHUFFLED record (250/0/400/100 out of order) parsed to the same sorted track and a name with a space (the chorus / first verse) round-tripped whole; the text grammar refused BadRecord five ways (bad header, non-mark line, missing name, leading-zero 007, non-numeric 1x); the bounds forwarded from markers.add by name (Duplicate on a repeated position, PastEnd at 501 past a 500-sample master, BadName on an oversized name, MarkersFull on max_markers+1 lines); a render into an 8-byte buffer refused Overflow.
obs tame_style_check exit 0 (bans clean); width-check exit 0; the new module carries asserts on both public functions, off the zero-assert ratchet.
loom witness=ales_cue_sheet_witness cases=6 markers=4 result=GREEN build=first
file lotus/cue_sheet.rye ALES22 module — the marker track travels as a format lotus-cue-sheet-v1 record, render/parse a fixed point.
file lotus/parse_int.rye symlink to canonical tally/parse_int.rye for strict decimal at the text edge.
file tools/ales_cue_sheet_witness.rish the witness proving ALES22 GREEN on metal.
file active-designing/20260814-fill-ales22-lotus-cue-sheet.md the self-approved design round for ALES22.
file lotus/README.md status line, rung bullet, and road-on updated for ALES22.
recommend keep-going ALES23 can name a selection (a marked span cut or gained as one), offer the choice of law where a crossfade meets a marked edit, or carry the cue sheet across the ALES0 audio wire as its own framed payload — all agent-doable, no custody gate. The audio-interface hardware write stays a paused research round, taken only on Keaton's word.
